<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Middleware on Dr. Soumadip Biswas</title><link>https://soumadip.github.io/tags/middleware/</link><description>Recent content in Middleware on Dr. Soumadip Biswas</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://soumadip.github.io/tags/middleware/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The Copilot's Blindspot: Critiquing AI-Generated Architectures</title><link>https://soumadip.github.io/viva/the-copilot-s-blindspot-critiquing-ai-generated-architectures/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://soumadip.github.io/viva/the-copilot-s-blindspot-critiquing-ai-generated-architectures/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="scenario-the-ai-generated-rate-limiter"&gt;Scenario: The AI-Generated Rate Limiter&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A recent graduate in their first technical interview is asked to implement a rate-limiting middleware using Redis to protect a public API. To speed things up, the candidate turns to an AI coding assistant. The LLM immediately outputs the following Python snippet:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-python" data-lang="python"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;check_rate_limit&lt;/span&gt;(user_id):
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; requests &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; redis&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;get(user_id)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; requests &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;and&lt;/span&gt; int(requests) &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;100&lt;/span&gt;:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# Rate limit exceeded&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; redis&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;incr(user_id)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;not&lt;/span&gt; requests:
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;# If this was the first request, set the expiration to 1 hour&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; redis&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;expire(user_id, &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;3600&lt;/span&gt;)
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; 
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The candidate looks at the code, notes that it is clean and readable, and submits it as their final answer.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>